cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite the accompanying article."
title: "Calibrating the Unrest Index for adult broiler video: the Hausdorff-distance percentile depends on the number of birds per frame"
abstract: >-
  Code and derived time series for a step-wise, rank-based re-analysis of the
  Unrest Index (Del Valle et al., 2021) on top-view adult-broiler video. Two
  modifications are evaluated: an instance-segmentation mask area centroid and
  the partial (percentile) Hausdorff distance. The central finding is the
  coupling between the useful percentile k and the number of birds per frame n,
  k*(n) ~= 100*(1 - 1/n): at n ~= 10 the medical-imaging HD95 is
  indistinguishable from the max and aggressive percentiles cost ordering.
